    "welcome": {
        "message": "A first look at the species range data for the California plant heat-vulnerability tool. 99 species are here as separate layers, from Calflora's climate-model distributions - toggle them in the layer menu.\n\nHow to read a layer: a cell's value is the number of times the species has been **observed** there. A cell the climate model finds suitable but where nobody has recorded the plant is **0**, and it is still inside the range - it is drawn pale rather than omitted. Cells outside the modelled climatic tolerance carry no value and are transparent. Across all 99 species only about 2% of in-range cells have ever been observed in, so a range reads as a broad pale extent with scattered red where the records are. That pattern is survey effort, not abundance.\n\nThe LOCA2 temperature projections are not loaded yet, so the exceedance-day calculation this tool is ultimately for is not available in this preview. The measured Tcrit and T50 values are not wired in yet either; they will arrive as provisional defaults ahead of the team's own publication, and will always be user-overridable.",
        "examples": [
            "Which species are on the map, and how large is each one's range?",
